§ `s 460 -- Advertising and dealing in counterfeit money, etc.`

-- (1) args: the thing is counterfeit money (s 448); the thing is a counterfeit token of value (s 448); advertises or offers by writing; purchases, obtains, negotiates or deals
#ASSERT `s 460(1) the person commits the offence of advertising and dealing in counterfeit money, etc.` `ccc14 Y` NOTHING TRUE FALSE EQUALS `ccc14 Y`
#ASSERT `s 460(1) the person commits the offence of advertising and dealing in counterfeit money, etc.` NOTHING `ccc14 Y` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `ccc14 Y`
#ASSERT `s 460(1) the person commits the offence of advertising and dealing in counterfeit money, etc.` NOTHING NOTHING TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 460(1) the person commits the offence of advertising and dealing in counterfeit money, etc.` NOTHING `ccc14 Y` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `ccc14 Y`
#ASSERT `s 460(1) the person commits the offence of advertising and dealing in counterfeit money, etc.` `ccc14 Y` NOTHING FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 460(1) the person commits the offence of advertising and dealing in counterfeit money, etc.` `ccc14 Y` `ccc14 Y` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 460(1) the class of the offence` EQUALS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
#ASSERT `s 460(1) the punishment` EQUALS LIST `ccc14 test indictable limb of years` 5, `ccc14 test summary limb with nothing stated`

-- (2) args: the offence is in respect of genuine coin or paper money with no value as money; knew it had no value; fraudulent intent
#ASSERT `s 460(2) the bar on conviction applies` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 460(2) the bar on conviction applies` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `ccc14 N`
#ASSERT `s 460(2) the bar on conviction applies` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `ccc14 Y`
#ASSERT `s 460(2) the bar on conviction applies` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `ccc14 Y`
#ASSERT `s 460(2) the bar on conviction applies` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `ccc14 Y`

§ `s 461 -- Special Provisions as to Proof`

-- (1) args: the offence relates to counterfeit money or tokens; not finished or perfected; do not copy exactly
#ASSERT `s 461(1) the offence is deemed complete` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `ccc14 Y`
#ASSERT `s 461(1) the offence is deemed complete` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `ccc14 Y`
#ASSERT `s 461(1) the offence is deemed complete` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 461(1) the offence is deemed complete` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (2) args: proceedings under this Part; signed by a designated examiner; states counterfeit, or genuine and current or not
#ASSERT `s 461(2) the certificate is evidence of its statements without proof of the signature` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `ccc14 Y`
#ASSERT `s 461(2) the certificate is evidence of its statements without proof of the signature` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 461(2) the certificate is evidence of its statements without proof of the signature` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 461(2) the certificate is evidence of its statements without proof of the signature` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (3) args: reasonable notice before the trial; a copy of the certificate
#ASSERT `s 461(3) the certificate is barred from being received in evidence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `ccc14 N`
#ASSERT `s 461(3) the certificate is barred from being received in evidence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `ccc14 Y`
#ASSERT `s 461(3) the certificate is barred from being received in evidence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `ccc14 Y`
#ASSERT `s 461(3) the certificate is barred from being received in evidence` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `ccc14 Y`

-- (4) args: the party is a party against whom the certificate is produced; the court has given leave
#ASSERT `s 461(4) the party may require the signer of the certificate to attend for cross-examination` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `ccc14 Y`
#ASSERT `s 461(4) the party may require the signer of the certificate to attend for cross-examination` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 461(4) the party may require the signer of the certificate to attend for cross-examination` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

